afk: park isolated-task commits on refs/omp/task/* instead of
refs/heads/omp/task/*.

Motivation: in a jj-colocated checkout, jj imports and manages
refs/heads/*. Upstream's transient task branches get imported by jj;
their post-merge deletion once made jj rebase the parent's commit stack
onto a stale bookmark and orphan every commit in between (the
abandoned-commits incident). Refs outside refs/heads/ are invisible to
jj import while every git command still resolves the short name
omp/task/<id> via git's refs/<name> lookup fallback.

What must survive a rebase:
- Every creation, lookup, deletion, and doc mention of the task branch
  uses the fully qualified refs/omp/task/<id> (git update-ref, not
  git branch) — grep upstream for "omp/task/" after rebasing; any new
  code path that mints refs/heads/omp/task/* reintroduces the bug.
- The ref must stay cherry-pickable and listable via
  `git for-each-ref refs/omp/task` (profile/rules/isolated-task-merge.md
  and the superpowers skill patches depend on that contract).
- Since 18.0.11 the VCS layer is native (gitoxide via
  @oh-my-pi/pi-natives/vcs) and its createBranch/deleteBranch hardcode
  refs/heads/, so worktree.ts carries its own gitUpdateRef/gitTryDeleteRef
  helpers shelling to `git update-ref` (the binary upstream still requires
  for fetch/push/clone). Detached temp worktrees are checked out at the
  resolved ref sha (resolveTaskRefSha) and the ref is advanced explicitly
  after each commit (advanceTaskRef). 18.x also added rescueTaskBranch
  (isolation-runner.ts, #8868) — it must probe/delete the HIDDEN ref, not
  refs/heads/.

Rebased 18.1.13 -> 18.2.10: upstream pruned
test/task/isolation-runner.test.ts wholesale (`chore: prune useless
tests`), so the test hunks this patch carried there are gone; the
worktree-jj-colocated test is unchanged. NestedRepoPatch now lives in
@oh-my-pi/pi-tui/tools/task.

Rebased 18.2.10 -> 18.6.0: upstream rewrote branch-mode capture
(commitToBranch, replayFilteredAgentCommits) to build every task commit
as a detached object through temporary indexes and write the ref once at
the end (createBranch(tip, force)); temporary worktrees are gone. The
re-cut follows the new shape: the agent-commit fetch lands on
refs/omp/task/<id>, and the final ref write is
gitUpdateRef(refs/omp/task/<id>, tip). advanceTaskRef/resolveTaskRefSha
were dropped with the temp worktrees they served (the "detached temp
worktrees" sentence above is historical). mergeTaskBranches,
cleanupTaskBranches and rescueTaskBranch hunks are unchanged in intent.
`grep omp/task/` over the rebased tree finds no other code path minting
refs/heads/omp/task/*.

